WEBVTT

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:12.900
S{*\c&HA6B8C1&}u{*\c&HABBCC5&}p{*\c&HB0C0C9&}r{*\c&HB5C5CC&}e{*\c&HB9C9D0&}m{*\c&HBECDD4&}e {*\c&HC8D6DB&}C{*\c&HCCDADF&}o{*\c&HD1DEE2&}u{*\c&HD6E2E6&}rt

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:18.740
Soga Kazuya, get out here!

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:21.270
Griffin Unit, ten minutes to air strike.

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:20.670
Eagle clear.

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:23.230
Fox, negative.

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:24.960
Griffin Unit, ten minutes to air strike.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:25.880
Griffin here. Roger that.

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:28.630
Griffin Unit, ten minutes to air strike.

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:28.630
It's clear!

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:40.010
Tossing hand grenade.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:41.800
Wait! They've got hostages.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:43.180
Request support!

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:43.220
Request support!

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:43.270
Request support!

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:43.350
Request support!

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:43.390
Request support!

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:11.000
We hereby issue the final verdict on defendant Soga Kazuya.

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:19.700
It is evident that the defendant committed crimes against humanity

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:21.260
during the fighting in Qhardistan.

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:29.010
Therefore, this war crimes court hereby sentences...

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:24.360
Strange... Why am I awake when everyone else is sleep-learning?

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:27.240
Lend me that clever little brain of yours.

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:33.770
Who are you?

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:41.290
Who is that updating my synchronization?

00:03:41.290 --> 00:03:42.860
You and me?

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:44.360
Huh?

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:47.630
We're doing this to clear both our names and Colonel Soga's!

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:50.180
Get the module into the vehicle!

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:03.110
This'll be our secret.

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:15.980
Last night, all of Public Security's systems went down for just about 1.8 seconds.

00:04:16.710 --> 00:04:18.840
Mistake? Error? Hacking?

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:20.930
We're investigating.

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:25.860
But there's a possibility that this Logicoma synced with something.

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:27.820
"Something"?

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:32.510
I want you to find out what—and how it's related to the system going down.

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:39.650
What freak would bother accessing an AI with an outdated neurochip,

00:04:39.650 --> 00:04:42.210
not to mention a conveyor that can only walk and talk?

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:47.450
In any case, we're leaving the others off and isolating this one.

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:49.180
I'd like you to investigate it too.

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:52.330
In other words, you're worried it was an inside job.

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:55.350
All right. I'll use a civilian facility.

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:59.690
I would have liked to go to an independent squad with this...

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:01.730
Still looking for the perfect personnel?

00:05:02.490 --> 00:05:05.440
It's <i>my</i> team. I won't take just anybody.

00:05:06.140 --> 00:05:08.820
People can get addicted to the carefree consultant life.

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:13.820
Or are you waiting to form it until it's a higher priority for the brass?

00:05:14.890 --> 00:05:19.490
If you want this squad to last, don't get overly ambitious.

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:29.340
Your parallel commands are randomized?

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:32.620
Is there a point to that?

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:35.660
It's so we can learn better.

00:05:39.030 --> 00:05:41.260
This is outside my system standards.

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:44.920
Can you explain the data you received verbally?

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:49.370
Um, I feel like it was something really important...

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:51.800
I see it was completely integrated.

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:55.490
Whoever did this, they're good.

00:05:55.490 --> 00:05:57.450
I feel sort of fluttery.

00:05:57.830 --> 00:06:00.240
There's no record of the infiltrator.

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:02.110
Not only were you fully integrated,

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:04.530
you got yourself bitten by false memories too.

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:06.710
I got bitten?!

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:11.420
Precious experience points!

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:19.480
Bingo.

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:23.710
Wow, that was inside me?! I'm amazing!

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:27.400
Yeah, yeah. They really are good.

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:29.490
I'm saying that as soldier,

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:32.240
killing your own countrymen is as low as you can sink!

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:33.210
What's this?

00:06:33.850 --> 00:06:37.530
We're doing it to prove our innocence, and the colonel's!

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:38.620
Just get the module—

00:06:57.390 --> 00:06:59.060
A traffic control error?

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:04.350
What, what, what?!

00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:06.190
Logicoma!

00:07:08.980 --> 00:07:09.780
Sheesh!

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:22.830
Why is everyone suddenly going crazy?!

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:42.980
Kusanagi Motoko...

00:08:42.980 --> 00:08:45.730
Kusanagi? The major with the 501?

00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:48.180
Pretty sure she's independent now.

00:08:48.980 --> 00:08:50.920
Call in all deployed personnel as reinforcements.

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:54.050
An assault?

00:08:54.670 --> 00:08:56.660
It's raining military-grade bullets.

00:08:56.660 --> 00:08:59.050
They took advantage of a traffic control error.

00:08:59.050 --> 00:09:02.810
Assuming you aren't setting me up, send backup.

00:09:03.580 --> 00:09:08.290
The attackers are battle cyborgs. One of them is Batou, the sleepless eye.

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:09.210
What?!

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:13.610
I found a strange code in the data planted in the Logicoma's AI.

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:16.140
So that's their objective.

00:09:16.970 --> 00:09:18.620
Put the Logicoma in self-defense mode.

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:20.640
I'll have backup there in fifteen minutes.

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:21.450
Fifteen?!

00:09:22.230 --> 00:09:25.640
The traffic network is being taken over.

00:09:25.640 --> 00:09:26.370
Report.

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:29.710
Domination expanding throughout the city.

00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:35.280
Well, hurry up and stop it!

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:36.960
We don't have enough processing speed.

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:39.950
Huh?

00:09:39.950 --> 00:09:40.840
Penetration increasing.

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:42.850
Defensive advance ineffective.

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:51.750
Locking down the airport now.

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:54.150
We have a malfunction in the new control system, cause unknown.

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:54.150
Divert all flights to surrounding airports.

00:09:58.050 --> 00:10:02.490
Both air-traffic control and the new street traffic system are affected.

00:10:02.490 --> 00:10:07.250
Eighty percent of the street system has been taken over by an outside operator.

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:15.700
This is crazy. What kind of outrageous system is our hacker using?!

00:10:16.820 --> 00:10:19.490
Major, fifteen minutes won't suffice.

00:10:19.490 --> 00:10:20.870
You're joking!

00:10:20.870 --> 00:10:22.430
This isn't an error.

00:10:22.940 --> 00:10:23.820
It's a crime.

00:10:28.780 --> 00:10:30.350
Large-scale domination?!

00:10:30.840 --> 00:10:32.680
Who has a system like that?!

00:10:42.850 --> 00:10:43.910
Hand me some weapons!

00:10:47.350 --> 00:10:48.850
Why are you empty?!

00:10:48.850 --> 00:10:50.540
I was being inspected.

00:10:51.160 --> 00:10:53.660
Guess I'll set up an ambush.

00:11:01.370 --> 00:11:03.180
You hear that, Borma?

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:04.970
Get it done in ten minutes.

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:07.140
Don't let Public Security use the de-parallelizing code.

00:11:07.580 --> 00:11:08.330
Borma!

00:11:11.730 --> 00:11:12.770
You bitch!

00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:49.890
Where do they get this stuff?!

00:11:53.390 --> 00:11:56.400
The area of the domination is still expanding, you know.

00:11:57.130 --> 00:11:59.610
The only solution is to get the module.

00:12:00.260 --> 00:12:03.470
Who are you? You've been spying on me since I left Public Security.

00:12:03.470 --> 00:12:08.320
I'm here to ask for help. I want you to trust me and hand over the conveyor.

00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:10.470
I recognize your voice from yesterday!

00:12:10.470 --> 00:12:13.790
Yes. I'm the one who infiltrated him.

00:12:26.010 --> 00:12:28.050
And Public Security's system going down?

00:12:28.050 --> 00:12:29.950
That wasn't me.

00:12:29.950 --> 00:12:32.500
That was the first move of the group

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:36.620
using a special military module to carry out a large-scale cyber operation.

00:12:36.620 --> 00:12:37.980
"Operation"?

00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:54.660
Here I go!

00:13:15.930 --> 00:13:16.820
Logicoma!

00:13:23.230 --> 00:13:27.490
The enemy stole the module's de-parallelizing code from me.

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:31.260
All I could do was replicate the code

00:13:31.260 --> 00:13:35.950
and copy it to an isolation-capable AI they couldn't interfere with.

00:13:37.060 --> 00:13:39.040
You, in other words.

00:13:39.340 --> 00:13:43.080
I knew it! I do carry an incredible secret!

00:13:43.610 --> 00:13:44.040
Indeed.

00:13:44.040 --> 00:13:44.760
Oh, dear.

00:13:45.500 --> 00:13:47.950
Logicoma, full speed. Get us to the exit!

00:13:47.950 --> 00:13:49.470
Aye aye, sir!

00:13:58.710 --> 00:13:59.310
Face front!

00:13:59.640 --> 00:14:01.020
And stop!

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:02.150
And stop!

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:03.150
And stop!

00:14:05.370 --> 00:14:06.070
Hey!

00:14:06.070 --> 00:14:06.940
Huh?

00:14:07.590 --> 00:14:08.240
Huh?

00:14:09.260 --> 00:14:10.320
Huh...

00:14:16.560 --> 00:14:17.160
Shield!

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:27.710
Huh?! I'm still in one piece.

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:52.090
Where'd this "military module" come from?

00:14:52.090 --> 00:14:57.180
It's a Mass Field-Hacking Unit jointly developed with seven leading companies from the old Silicon Valley.

00:14:57.930 --> 00:15:01.460
Military joint production? Are you an American agent?

00:15:02.900 --> 00:15:05.410
I'm Special Forces.

00:15:05.410 --> 00:15:09.260
My code name is "VV". I'm supporting you in hope of your cooperation.

00:15:12.980 --> 00:15:15.170
Great. Now we've got two enemies.

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:20.950
So they sent her to retrieve the module.

00:15:20.950 --> 00:15:22.680
But don't let her throw you off.

00:15:22.680 --> 00:15:26.690
All we have to do is destroy the Public Security machine, and it's checkmate.

00:15:27.690 --> 00:15:29.150
How's the domination coming?

00:15:29.670 --> 00:15:31.800
We're close to target values.

00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:33.650
We won't let 'em get away with anything else.

00:15:33.970 --> 00:15:36.620
Get me a line and patch me to the colonel.

00:15:37.600 --> 00:15:40.870
This war crimes court hereby sentences...

00:15:49.580 --> 00:15:51.260
Colonel Soga, how dare you?!

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:52.920
Who the hell are you?!

00:15:53.290 --> 00:15:56.430
The Administrative Vice-Minister of Defense. l want to talk to that man!

00:15:56.750 --> 00:16:02.010
Vice-Minister Kasuga. I'm flattered by your concern.

00:16:02.010 --> 00:16:05.380
But I create my own circumstances.

00:16:05.380 --> 00:16:05.980
Excuse me?

00:16:06.220 --> 00:16:09.320
Those who obstruct my Net will disappear from this city.

00:16:13.400 --> 00:16:16.570
I only desire one thing...

00:16:22.580 --> 00:16:25.210
For the truth about our circumstances to be known!

00:16:34.940 --> 00:16:37.610
Aramaki, I assume you've heard of Soga?

00:16:37.610 --> 00:16:42.260
Soga Kazuya, the war criminal in the Qhardistan massacre, correct?

00:16:42.260 --> 00:16:47.530
He's the man behind this traffic chaos.

00:16:47.530 --> 00:16:51.190
He's still connected to the Net even after we tossed him in an isolation cell.

00:16:51.390 --> 00:16:53.420
Can't the great Section 9 stop him?!

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:57.050
He's on an independent line via military satellite.

00:16:57.050 --> 00:17:00.670
We'd have to open a hole in our tactical defenses: either kill the line with him,

00:17:00.670 --> 00:17:02.660
or shoot down the satellite.

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:03.950
Out of the question!

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:07.560
Then our hands are tied for the moment.

00:17:07.560 --> 00:17:10.730
Even with all Home Affairs and civilian AIs working at full capacity,

00:17:10.730 --> 00:17:16.720
we wouldn't have the processing power to break his command and take back the traffic control systems.

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:21.410
They made him a scapegoat when he refused to testify in court.

00:17:21.410 --> 00:17:26.820
I did what I could to commute his sentence.

00:17:26.820 --> 00:17:28.600
But I never thought he'd mobilize his unit!

00:17:29.240 --> 00:17:31.530
His motive is clear, anyway.

00:17:31.530 --> 00:17:36.070
To an honest soldier, a postwar military purge is a state betrayal.

00:17:38.070 --> 00:17:40.160
Well, have a seat.

00:17:40.930 --> 00:17:43.910
Where did his unit get those weapons?

00:17:43.910 --> 00:17:46.590
The lower-ranking NCOs are on strike right now,

00:17:46.590 --> 00:17:49.290
so it wouldn't surprise anyone if a whole arsenal disappeared.

00:17:51.650 --> 00:17:54.170
One last thing, then: what's he after?

00:17:57.450 --> 00:18:00.380
He's demanding access to a military database...

00:18:01.950 --> 00:18:04.180
...called "Pandora".

00:18:04.180 --> 00:18:06.300
State secrets?

00:18:07.240 --> 00:18:11.730
Does he mean to bring the details of an Army operation before the war crimes court?

00:18:12.770 --> 00:18:14.070
That's not all.

00:18:15.500 --> 00:18:18.450
He wants the Army's and Public Security's dirty laundry to be publicly revealed

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:22.610
in exchange for this city's 20 million cars and the people in them.

00:18:22.970 --> 00:18:27.290
He wants Japan itself to be judged just as he was?

00:18:27.560 --> 00:18:32.710
Other countries would use war crimes as a pretext for all sorts of demands.

00:18:33.310 --> 00:18:35.710
We might as well be under occupation again.

00:18:36.190 --> 00:18:41.820
As the war's greatest losers, our country would be the world's puppet state.

00:18:41.820 --> 00:18:45.900
It doesn't even bear discussing! We'll never give in to that demand!

00:18:45.900 --> 00:18:48.680
Are you speaking on behalf of Home Affairs?

00:18:48.920 --> 00:18:51.050
N-No! But...

00:18:56.840 --> 00:18:58.610
Colonel Soga Kazuya?

00:18:58.610 --> 00:19:03.070
He commanded an op in Qhardistan that earned him high praise.

00:19:03.360 --> 00:19:06.220
Then he was accused of conducting a massacre during the op

00:19:06.220 --> 00:19:10.190
and convicted as a war criminal. He's currently in custody.

00:19:10.190 --> 00:19:13.520
A hero during the war, and a criminal afterward.

00:19:13.520 --> 00:19:17.770
And Soga's sympathizers are using the module to force his release?

00:19:18.400 --> 00:19:19.090
Major—

00:19:19.400 --> 00:19:23.360
She's an informant. I brought her in on a provisional basis.

00:19:23.820 --> 00:19:25.590
What exactly is this "module"?

00:19:26.700 --> 00:19:31.060
It creates processing power on the level of a giant nationwide system.

00:19:31.730 --> 00:19:36.830
They must have used it to parallelize something low-capacity in huge quantities.

00:19:37.450 --> 00:19:38.810
Your opinion?

00:19:38.810 --> 00:19:40.570
I agree with Major Kusanagi.

00:19:40.970 --> 00:19:44.030
And is your objective to retrieve the module?

00:19:44.250 --> 00:19:46.430
Or destroy it.

00:19:46.430 --> 00:19:52.910
The most effective method is to use the code I evacuated into your AI

00:19:52.910 --> 00:19:56.060
from somewhere free of enemy interference.

00:19:56.060 --> 00:19:58.040
Why was it stolen in the first place?

00:19:58.650 --> 00:20:04.070
The module was a model brought here to establish a top-secret joint project with Japan.

00:20:04.070 --> 00:20:08.970
I take it your colleagues are investigating the theft behind the curtains?

00:20:09.350 --> 00:20:11.300
I'll leave that to your imagination.

00:20:12.010 --> 00:20:15.160
Along with how you pinpointed the enemy's smuggling point?

00:20:16.210 --> 00:20:19.000
Both issues are the purview of the Administrative Vice-Minister of Defense,

00:20:19.000 --> 00:20:23.020
but he didn't mention them when I spoke to him just now.

00:20:23.020 --> 00:20:26.090
Evidently something's being hushed up.

00:20:26.090 --> 00:20:31.520
Another reason I want you to tell the Ministry of Home Affairs to give my squad top priority.

00:20:31.520 --> 00:20:33.870
Since when do you have a squad?!

00:20:34.570 --> 00:20:39.630
I'm about to form one. Based on skill, with no ranks, and given top priority.

00:20:39.980 --> 00:20:43.210
Bad idea! Special forces teams aren't mercenaries!

00:20:43.210 --> 00:20:45.660
If you take advantage of a disaster for your own gain,

00:20:45.660 --> 00:20:48.840
the defense world will treat you like a vulture!

00:20:48.840 --> 00:20:50.800
I'm not interested in teams out for money

00:20:51.300 --> 00:20:55.770
or ministry bigwigs gunning for postwar concessions.

00:20:56.030 --> 00:20:59.290
Tell me this: how are the Home Affairs higher-ups?

00:20:59.290 --> 00:21:02.420
Having themselves an "elite panic" with the Ministry of Defense.

00:21:02.420 --> 00:21:06.390
They're afraid the public will panic if word gets out,

00:21:06.390 --> 00:21:09.550
so other than a few of my units, they won't order anyone to act.

00:21:09.550 --> 00:21:11.990
We're the only ones who can act right now.

00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:18.370
A team formed on a fixed standard that will be necessary everywhere and in every age.

00:21:29.990 --> 00:21:32.010
So it's finally taking off.

00:21:58.940 --> 00:22:01.020
Whoops, survived again.

00:22:02.500 --> 00:22:05.010
Playing Russian roulette in VR?

00:22:10.190 --> 00:22:13.980
Do you reproduce the sensation of the bullet penetrating your cranium too?

00:22:13.980 --> 00:22:15.390
You've got a sickness.

00:22:16.770 --> 00:22:19.870
Kusanagi from the 501! When did you sneak in here?!

00:22:19.870 --> 00:22:25.340
I'm independent. The op in Qhardistan, the American Army module, and Soga...

00:22:26.110 --> 00:22:29.830
Tell me what you know, or take a real-life bullet. Your choice.

00:22:29.830 --> 00:22:31.660
Hold on! Why come to me?

00:22:32.310 --> 00:22:34.810
You served under Soga in Qhardistan.

00:22:34.810 --> 00:22:38.730
There's a record of Ishikawa calling you on your private line.

00:22:38.730 --> 00:22:43.480
Hey, I turned down the job with the 78th! The pay wasn't good enough.

00:22:43.480 --> 00:22:47.320
The Marines' ace sniper turned into a compulsive gambler after the war?

00:22:47.320 --> 00:22:51.430
Is that why your unit's leave-time budget's been cooked to high hell?

00:22:51.430 --> 00:22:52.720
How did you know—

00:22:54.170 --> 00:22:57.580
If your postwar days are about turning your life into cash,

00:22:57.580 --> 00:23:00.140
I'll play your game.

00:23:00.140 --> 00:23:04.170
Join my spec ops team in the next five seconds,

00:23:04.170 --> 00:23:07.770
or the money you embezzled gets transferred to Maritime Command.

00:23:08.390 --> 00:23:09.820
Bitch.

00:23:11.080 --> 00:23:12.910
I'll pay you a salary.

00:23:17.540 --> 00:23:20.330
Divert everyone before we lose the whole system.

00:23:54.300 --> 00:23:55.780
So you're the MP?

00:23:56.220 --> 00:23:59.350
What'd she threaten you with to bring you in?

00:23:59.350 --> 00:24:01.270
Oh, I volunteered.

00:24:01.270 --> 00:24:04.480
I've been waiting for the Major to start up her team.

00:24:04.480 --> 00:24:06.370
You're one messed-up guy.

00:24:13.550 --> 00:24:16.740
How can you control this with the domination going on?

00:24:16.740 --> 00:24:19.430
This antique has some special specifications.

00:24:19.430 --> 00:24:23.340
It's not in the same class as your friend's old clunker there!

00:24:30.010 --> 00:24:34.150
Since we can't cut Soga's Net, we'll have to physically seize the module.

00:24:34.490 --> 00:24:38.430
This facility is the most likely candidate for our enemy's base.

00:24:38.430 --> 00:24:40.770
I see. You'll only give us our target's location.

00:24:40.770 --> 00:24:43.600
You don't want to get your own hands dirty.

00:24:43.600 --> 00:24:45.620
I'm what you'd call a neat freak.

00:24:45.940 --> 00:24:49.070
An old communications equipment company, eh?

00:24:49.070 --> 00:24:53.250
Not much for a sniper to do if they're holed up in a server room.

00:24:53.860 --> 00:24:58.090
Don't worry, I'll smoke out plenty of targets for you.

00:25:09.910 --> 00:25:11.020
Bingo? Seriously?

00:25:11.340 --> 00:25:14.530
Just one squad, and they get their own ground support chopper...

00:25:15.430 --> 00:25:17.030
Good grief.

00:25:44.000 --> 00:25:45.250
We're going in, Logicoma.

00:25:45.250 --> 00:25:48.060
Huh? But I'm not done with the sensors...

00:25:48.540 --> 00:25:50.400
What?! Really?!

00:25:55.660 --> 00:25:56.430
Safe...

00:25:56.430 --> 00:25:57.880
You're slow!

00:26:06.890 --> 00:26:08.270
Paz, status?

00:26:08.270 --> 00:26:11.290
Not sure if you could say it went well, but I'm in.

00:26:11.800 --> 00:26:15.170
So are we. Report back if you find the module.

00:26:15.810 --> 00:26:16.860
Let's do this.

00:26:16.860 --> 00:26:17.830
It's useless!

00:26:29.010 --> 00:26:30.500
A barrier maze?

00:26:34.500 --> 00:26:36.010
This processing speed...

00:26:36.970 --> 00:26:41.320
You people can't stop my Net.

00:26:43.370 --> 00:26:47.480
In about an hour, Pandora's lid will open.

00:26:47.480 --> 00:26:51.040
It's impossible to stop me before then.

00:26:51.370 --> 00:26:54.250
Are you willing to go this far to get your revenge on this country?!

00:26:56.630 --> 00:26:58.670
I'm uncovering the truth.

00:27:53.420 --> 00:27:56.750
The op to move the refugees in Qhardistan

00:27:56.750 --> 00:27:59.610
was the 78th Composite Unit's final mission.

00:27:59.610 --> 00:28:02.220
Which was an extermination op you led.

00:28:02.220 --> 00:28:03.340
No!

00:28:03.800 --> 00:28:04.360
This is...

00:28:09.770 --> 00:28:12.640
They were unarmed refugees.

00:28:12.640 --> 00:28:16.740
Afterward, a conglomerate occupied their land.

00:28:16.740 --> 00:28:20.500
Someone ordered their slaughter to benefit the national interest.

00:28:35.960 --> 00:28:37.220
Give me water!

00:29:03.550 --> 00:29:06.090
This is the first step.

00:29:06.750 --> 00:29:12.430
I'll put all the nations who led the world into war in that same position.

00:29:12.430 --> 00:29:14.670
Soga! You've been inf—

00:29:22.110 --> 00:29:23.060
Soga?

00:29:27.860 --> 00:29:31.320
This is... a gap in the maze, maybe?

00:29:31.640 --> 00:29:35.130
How did she leave the barrier maze? No—she didn't.

00:29:43.690 --> 00:29:45.570
Soga can't see me?

00:29:45.570 --> 00:29:47.610
I did manage to land in a gap.

00:29:57.870 --> 00:29:59.750
An accident-prevention AI?!

00:30:00.500 --> 00:30:03.430
He's parallelized all the AIs in Japan's traffic network!

00:30:26.460 --> 00:30:28.280
That was close.

00:30:28.280 --> 00:30:32.140
My barrier won't last long. Let's hurry.

00:30:32.580 --> 00:30:36.640
It's been three minutes since we lost contact with Major Kusanagi.

00:30:37.010 --> 00:30:38.970
Call from the Ministry of Defense.

00:30:38.970 --> 00:30:42.150
A DoS attack on the Pandora barrier began four minutes ago.

00:30:43.110 --> 00:30:44.950
We can't keep up with it.

00:30:46.540 --> 00:30:50.150
Sounds like it was a mistake to give Public Security free rein!

00:30:50.150 --> 00:30:54.060
You invited this by carelessly stirring Soga up!

00:30:56.690 --> 00:30:59.200
Major! Are you all right? What's the situation?

00:30:59.600 --> 00:31:03.980
Soga took over the traffic control system through the module.

00:31:03.980 --> 00:31:07.670
But the threat to kill it we didn't release Pandora was fake.

00:31:08.490 --> 00:31:10.840
He intends to use the vast system power he's gained

00:31:10.840 --> 00:31:12.930
to break Pandora wide open.

00:31:14.280 --> 00:31:15.430
I see...

00:31:16.810 --> 00:31:19.720
In that case, there are steps we can take.

00:31:19.720 --> 00:31:22.640
You keep working to recover the module.

00:31:26.990 --> 00:31:28.270
Nice timing!

00:31:28.760 --> 00:31:31.430
The deal with the government should be a bluff.

00:31:31.430 --> 00:31:33.030
Colonel Soga went too far.

00:31:33.600 --> 00:31:36.850
This started as a plan for the Vice-Minister to sell Pandora!

00:31:36.850 --> 00:31:39.690
We can't survive turning the whole world against us!

00:31:40.770 --> 00:31:42.990
If you've got cold feet, run.

00:31:42.990 --> 00:31:44.460
Nobody'll stop you.

00:31:44.940 --> 00:31:46.690
Negotiate a deal or whatever.

00:31:46.690 --> 00:31:47.710
I sure will!

00:31:49.720 --> 00:31:51.560
If you're in this for money, run without a fight.

00:32:00.120 --> 00:32:03.710
Hey! Home Affairs just gave us money!

00:32:03.710 --> 00:32:05.100
Give it to someone who cares!

00:32:06.790 --> 00:32:07.610
We're withdrawing.

00:32:07.900 --> 00:32:09.630
I'll buy some time.

00:32:09.630 --> 00:32:14.150
The colonel didn't even wait to clear the 78th's name.

00:32:14.370 --> 00:32:15.670
Why do you figure that is?

00:32:17.110 --> 00:32:18.280
Kasuga!

00:32:20.070 --> 00:32:22.140
They've made him a scapegoat!

00:32:22.140 --> 00:32:22.930
Let's go!

00:32:23.520 --> 00:32:25.690
I'll meet up with you once I've hindered them sufficiently.

00:32:25.690 --> 00:32:27.130
Do it fast.

00:32:27.590 --> 00:32:29.230
Paz, do you read me?

00:32:29.230 --> 00:32:30.360
More or less.

00:32:30.360 --> 00:32:32.360
Do you know an intelligence man named Ishikawa?

00:32:32.360 --> 00:32:33.260
Sure do.

00:32:36.730 --> 00:32:39.410
If you find him, use a cable to get him to the cyber lobby.

00:32:39.410 --> 00:32:40.070
Roger!

00:32:40.580 --> 00:32:42.850
I'm hanging up before they detect our line.

00:32:43.080 --> 00:32:47.360
Shit. The colonel's set up the domination, but they're still roaming free!

00:32:51.920 --> 00:32:53.090
Don't underestimate me.

00:32:53.090 --> 00:32:58.110
I can locate even a super-wizard-class hacker if they make a call during domination!

00:32:58.110 --> 00:33:00.290
The Major's got business with you.

00:33:00.290 --> 00:33:03.490
Let me connect you, and nobody gets hurt.

00:33:03.970 --> 00:33:07.540
Try it, kiddo. I'll play with you.

00:33:18.640 --> 00:33:21.140
Be a good boy, and you won't get hurt.

00:33:22.220 --> 00:33:23.310
You mean you won't.

00:33:25.470 --> 00:33:28.140
She was playing me with that call? Damn gorilla woman!

00:33:30.550 --> 00:33:32.820
Who are you calling a gorilla?

00:33:36.120 --> 00:33:37.740
Major Kusanagi!

00:33:43.950 --> 00:33:46.330
Planning to stick me with a virus?

00:33:46.330 --> 00:33:48.940
The opposite. I think you're already infected.

00:33:48.940 --> 00:33:49.620
What?

00:33:50.310 --> 00:33:54.380
It's a makeshift vaccine, so you'll have to put up with any bugs.

00:34:03.370 --> 00:34:05.540
I've lost contact with Ishikawa.

00:34:05.540 --> 00:34:06.770
I'll go.

00:34:07.330 --> 00:34:10.840
I'll take the module and go on ahead. We rendezvous at the trap!

00:34:10.840 --> 00:34:12.060
Roger!

00:34:12.470 --> 00:34:13.130
Drive.

00:34:15.700 --> 00:34:18.360
Shit. You, Saito?!

00:34:19.310 --> 00:34:22.280
We're all pros here. No hard feelings.

00:34:22.640 --> 00:34:24.990
It you're a pro, join the side that pays best.

00:34:25.430 --> 00:34:28.790
Home Affairs paid us. I'll give you a triple share.

00:34:29.270 --> 00:34:31.520
Take it from my account!

00:34:31.520 --> 00:34:32.540
For real?!

00:34:41.370 --> 00:34:42.010
Ishikawa!

00:34:42.280 --> 00:34:44.260
C'mon, let's get back to guarding the module.

00:34:44.490 --> 00:34:45.510
Don't move.

00:34:46.970 --> 00:34:48.930
Hey! Ishikawa?!

00:34:52.040 --> 00:34:52.850
Major!

00:34:54.180 --> 00:34:57.780
They all left. Only one car stayed behind.

00:34:58.950 --> 00:34:59.810
It didn't work!

00:34:59.810 --> 00:35:01.780
Damn, they pulled out already?

00:35:02.140 --> 00:35:03.500
They've got good judgment.

00:35:04.140 --> 00:35:07.490
Paz, you go in VV's car. I'll go with the Logicoma!

00:35:12.650 --> 00:35:13.500
Saito!

00:35:27.310 --> 00:35:29.710
You wired them money?!

00:35:29.710 --> 00:35:32.770
Why would you swallow the enemy's bluff so easily?

00:35:33.210 --> 00:35:35.950
This is the result of our negotiation with Soga.

00:35:35.950 --> 00:35:38.840
We planned to put the money toward the Economic Amnesty Act,

00:35:38.840 --> 00:35:42.740
but it came from vet pensions that got slashed in the Army budget cuts.

00:35:43.060 --> 00:35:47.140
Do you honestly think that's what they're after?!

00:35:47.140 --> 00:35:50.450
Just whose cause are we supposed to be working for here?

00:35:50.450 --> 00:35:54.580
The funds will be traced, and the Department of Defense is taking responsibility.

00:35:54.580 --> 00:35:56.960
Our people stay out of this, got it?

00:36:01.450 --> 00:36:03.700
Did you check up on the enemy's parallel circuitry?

00:36:03.700 --> 00:36:07.890
The on-board AIs of 20 million vehicles in this city are in enemy control.

00:36:08.190 --> 00:36:09.500
Including my car.

00:36:09.500 --> 00:36:12.600
The system is so overpowered we can hardly manage to move one chopper.

00:36:13.820 --> 00:36:18.310
But there is a way to turn the tables, if only temporarily.

00:36:18.310 --> 00:36:19.270
Tell me.

00:36:36.020 --> 00:36:37.580
Charge!

00:36:40.860 --> 00:36:42.300
Here already?!

00:36:46.220 --> 00:36:47.580
Logicoma, the tires!

00:36:56.810 --> 00:36:58.230
Cut between them. You take right!

00:37:13.310 --> 00:37:16.540
A car?! How can they move during the domination?

00:37:17.960 --> 00:37:19.410
Here we go, Paz.

00:37:34.230 --> 00:37:35.770
He's taken over my car!

00:37:36.920 --> 00:37:39.540
"Special specifications", my ass!

00:37:39.540 --> 00:37:42.940
He quit everything to focus some crazy pressure on me!

00:37:42.940 --> 00:37:43.820
It's too much!

00:37:45.220 --> 00:37:46.190
Ishikawa!

00:37:46.590 --> 00:37:49.070
Damn gorilla woman's calling.

00:37:54.790 --> 00:37:56.040
Ishikawa?

00:38:01.400 --> 00:38:04.400
Shit. Never figured the colonel would try to brain-fry me!

00:38:04.400 --> 00:38:06.800
I can't believe it—did he really?!

00:38:07.520 --> 00:38:10.890
We're about to find out what the truth is.

00:38:14.850 --> 00:38:16.770
I have control!

00:38:22.390 --> 00:38:24.440
Ishikawa's cooperating with 'em?

00:38:43.900 --> 00:38:45.380
Saito!

00:38:45.610 --> 00:38:48.340
Sorry, lady, but they sweetened the pot.

00:38:50.200 --> 00:38:51.180
Good work, Saito!

00:38:53.560 --> 00:38:55.510
We're almost to the trap.

00:38:55.930 --> 00:38:57.390
Once we get there...

00:38:57.390 --> 00:38:58.890
We win!

00:39:00.140 --> 00:39:02.940
You damn gambling-freak mercenary!

00:39:25.860 --> 00:39:29.510
Huh? I can't see them anymore.

00:39:39.580 --> 00:39:40.930
This makes no sense.

00:39:41.870 --> 00:39:42.890
Where are they?!

00:39:44.010 --> 00:39:46.860
Five minutes to infiltration of Pandora.

00:39:49.510 --> 00:39:53.930
There's no record that I've been hacked, so why did they vanish?!

00:39:53.930 --> 00:39:56.570
They didn't overwrite your vision.

00:39:56.820 --> 00:39:58.140
Can you move?!

00:39:58.140 --> 00:40:01.060
I lost my right arm, but don't worry; we're still in the game.

00:40:01.060 --> 00:40:02.940
So what was their trick?

00:40:04.110 --> 00:40:07.570
They used our own skills to take us out. Slick of them.

00:40:07.570 --> 00:40:09.340
It's an old type of optical camouflage holograph.

00:40:10.570 --> 00:40:12.990
I'd have missed it if we weren't going so slowly.

00:40:12.990 --> 00:40:14.590
I'll send you the location.

00:40:14.870 --> 00:40:18.050
Securing the module is top priority. We're out of time.

00:40:19.260 --> 00:40:20.010
They figured it out?

00:40:21.540 --> 00:40:23.480
They're damn persistent!

00:40:53.480 --> 00:40:53.960
Fire!

00:40:53.960 --> 00:40:54.260
Aye!

00:41:27.160 --> 00:41:30.360
We can't go fast, so it'll take us a bit.

00:41:30.360 --> 00:41:31.540
No problem.

00:41:31.540 --> 00:41:33.580
Logicoma, you stay there.

00:41:33.580 --> 00:41:35.240
Wait until we get to you!

00:41:41.370 --> 00:41:42.750
Skilled as always.

00:41:42.750 --> 00:41:48.080
But you're not the only one good at infiltrating vision, 501 Major...

00:41:48.080 --> 00:41:49.400
No, just "Major" now.

00:42:08.060 --> 00:42:08.810
Paz!

00:42:10.110 --> 00:42:12.210
VV, get the module, fast!

00:42:16.750 --> 00:42:19.130
Ten seconds to infiltration of Pandora.

00:42:19.420 --> 00:42:20.320
Nine...

00:42:20.320 --> 00:42:21.280
Eight...

00:42:21.280 --> 00:42:22.310
Seven...

00:42:22.310 --> 00:42:23.100
Six...

00:42:36.570 --> 00:42:38.410
Slow Down for Roadblocks

00:42:42.330 --> 00:42:47.020
We set up 317 roadblocks, from Wards 1 through 38.

00:42:47.020 --> 00:42:48.410
Do we keep going?

00:42:48.770 --> 00:42:52.120
Mobilize all forces and put up as many as you can.

00:42:52.120 --> 00:42:56.400
We'll tie up all vehicles' on-board computers with accident-avoidance processes.

00:42:56.400 --> 00:42:57.880
The fate of our nation is at stake.

00:42:58.910 --> 00:43:00.880
I feel bad for the MLIT,

00:43:00.880 --> 00:43:04.340
but I'm going to cause the worst gridlock in thirty years.

00:43:14.040 --> 00:43:16.110
Aramaki from Public Security?

00:43:20.630 --> 00:43:22.200
This is his doing?

00:43:38.550 --> 00:43:39.340
Paz!

00:43:50.660 --> 00:43:51.930
You're too late.

00:43:52.920 --> 00:43:55.590
Soga's opening up Pandora as we speak.

00:43:55.590 --> 00:43:58.070
Nope. His power is down.

00:43:59.560 --> 00:44:04.030
Public Security's stopped more than thirty percent of the vehicles that were in motion.

00:44:15.710 --> 00:44:19.170
Both you and Colonel Soga had been deliberately infected.

00:45:00.570 --> 00:45:04.050
There is no "truth" about that refugee transport op.

00:45:04.830 --> 00:45:07.850
You killed those people and ordered an air strike.

00:45:08.760 --> 00:45:12.720
You did it because all the "refugees" you were trying to safeguard

00:45:12.720 --> 00:45:14.730
were armed guerrillas.

00:45:22.880 --> 00:45:25.090
It's the MOD's responsibility now.

00:45:25.090 --> 00:45:28.570
Either do something about him, or destroy Pandora right now!

00:45:28.860 --> 00:45:30.930
Obviously out of the question!

00:45:32.570 --> 00:45:35.290
Because you want me to open Pandora?

00:45:36.030 --> 00:45:36.500
What?

00:45:38.660 --> 00:45:39.460
Don't!

00:45:42.190 --> 00:45:43.210
You bastard!

00:45:45.780 --> 00:45:47.340
Wait! Don't shoot!

00:45:48.520 --> 00:45:52.490
It was the Administrative Vice-Minister who gave me the module.

00:45:52.490 --> 00:45:55.060
That agent's objective is the same.

00:45:55.060 --> 00:45:58.140
Make sure you don't use the de-parallelizing code.

00:45:58.370 --> 00:45:59.230
What?

00:46:01.180 --> 00:46:02.980
I can't stop the infiltration.

00:46:03.360 --> 00:46:04.900
This is the only way!

00:46:05.940 --> 00:46:06.900
Stop!

00:46:15.620 --> 00:46:17.640
I gave you a copy of the vaccine.

00:46:17.640 --> 00:46:20.890
It's imperfect, but you'll be able to tell which memories are false.

00:46:21.820 --> 00:46:25.700
It's unlikely we'll be able to eradicate them, but I'll give you a hand.

00:46:26.150 --> 00:46:27.210
Not interested.

00:46:29.320 --> 00:46:33.720
It's the only memory that lets me feel like I'm not just a dog trained to kill!

00:46:37.250 --> 00:46:39.340
You're just a whiny bitch, then.

00:46:41.640 --> 00:46:43.100
What happened, Major?!

00:46:43.100 --> 00:46:45.960
It's over. Send a rescue squad.

00:46:45.960 --> 00:46:48.110
What do you mean, "over"?!

00:46:48.650 --> 00:46:50.070
Pandora's been infiltrated!

00:46:50.510 --> 00:46:53.570
The data's being leaked to a different Net than Soga's!

00:46:58.350 --> 00:46:59.660
Step away from the module!

00:47:09.860 --> 00:47:13.430
Don't resist. I feel an affinity with you.

00:47:14.540 --> 00:47:19.450
You, who haven't had a flesh-and-blood body for as long as you can remember.

00:47:28.230 --> 00:47:29.430
You bitch...

00:47:39.890 --> 00:47:42.470
That attack barrier is meaningless.

00:47:45.250 --> 00:47:49.090
My brain has to be synchronized, like his.

00:47:53.120 --> 00:47:55.050
A neurochip?

00:47:55.050 --> 00:47:56.340
You're...

00:47:57.740 --> 00:47:59.810
I must find out where it came from.

00:48:00.170 --> 00:48:06.690
This thing which infected me and gave me true self-awareness.

00:48:06.920 --> 00:48:12.280
Even if I have to access every institution in the world and unearth their secrets,

00:48:12.650 --> 00:48:13.740
I won't hesitate.

00:48:28.590 --> 00:48:32.170
You're an artificial intelligence pretending to be human...

00:48:33.450 --> 00:48:34.840
What for?

00:48:35.710 --> 00:48:38.620
I just have to know.

00:48:38.620 --> 00:48:45.810
My Ghost whi...spered... that... to... me...

00:48:47.890 --> 00:48:48.810
Ghost...

00:48:54.930 --> 00:48:55.740
Huh?

00:48:56.010 --> 00:48:57.800
A certain intelligence agency admitted

00:48:57.800 --> 00:49:02.140
that one of its AIs was infected with an unknown virus on the Net

00:49:02.140 --> 00:49:04.360
and began acting outside of their control.

00:49:04.940 --> 00:49:09.980
And it absconded with the module, then manipulated the Vice-Minister.

00:49:09.980 --> 00:49:13.670
He made too many dangerous deals during the war.

00:49:14.200 --> 00:49:17.660
He intended to sell the contents of Pandora and flee the country.

00:49:17.660 --> 00:49:22.640
That's why he manipulated Soga and sent in a team of his own pawns.

00:49:22.640 --> 00:49:27.170
But Soga seized control of the situation, so the AI planned a recovery strategy.

00:49:27.170 --> 00:49:30.060
"A rogue AI did it all"... How very convenient.

00:49:30.620 --> 00:49:34.380
Even if it's half true, I'm sure they let things lie to try to profit from her.

00:49:34.380 --> 00:49:39.010
Though it seems they're not the only ones to try to profit from this.

00:49:39.010 --> 00:49:41.070
<i>You're</i> the one who came to me.

00:49:41.270 --> 00:49:47.000
With these results, your long-awaited top priority team is a fait accompli.

00:49:47.260 --> 00:49:51.020
Want to re-register as part of Section 9?

00:49:51.020 --> 00:49:54.990
They'll cancel the registration if you can't get enough people together.

00:49:54.990 --> 00:49:56.010
No thanks.

00:49:56.690 --> 00:49:59.710
I appreciate your help with the paperwork, though.

00:50:18.620 --> 00:50:21.360
It'll close in five minutes. Decide before then.

00:50:21.800 --> 00:50:26.300
Sit there and get sentenced in one of the speed-trials the system loves,

00:50:26.300 --> 00:50:27.800
or join my squad.

00:50:29.030 --> 00:50:32.790
You say that to everyone you've been in shooting matches with?

00:50:32.790 --> 00:50:35.750
I can only get people infected with the memory virus released.

00:50:36.510 --> 00:50:38.970
Though those three are the ones I want anyway.

00:50:39.880 --> 00:50:42.720
They'll accept that after we just picked a fight with the government?

00:50:43.050 --> 00:50:48.680
Maybe, provided I, Section 9, and a certain country's intelligence agency testify about the false memories.

00:50:49.230 --> 00:50:51.420
Ishikawa and Borma agreed.

00:50:51.420 --> 00:50:55.370
As for Saito, when I paid him a little visit before he could go to ground,

00:50:55.370 --> 00:50:58.230
he begged me to let him join.

00:51:00.810 --> 00:51:02.390
You're some piece of work.

00:51:03.200 --> 00:51:05.740
